      "clause_ids": ["POL-RD-22", "POL-RD-24"],
      "relies_on": "trip_record.derived.v7.deviation.deviation_km",
      "asserted_weight": 1.0
    },
    {
      "text": "POL-RD-23's traffic justification is met. EV-ADVIS-05011-01 is an LTA traffic advisory of type ACCIDENT, and ACCIDENT is inside the policy's admissible 'incident' vocabulary; its road field is the Pan-Island Expressway (PIE), which is one of the roads the recommended route uses (trip_record.optimal_route_via: KJE, PIE, CTE, Outram Road); its validity window 07:44:37 to 08:54:37 brackets the whole trip window 07:54:37 to 08:29:07; and its own text directs drivers to avoid lanes 1 and 2 on PIE at that time, which is exactly why the driver left PIE. The record carries nothing putting this incident off the recommended route — the derived intersects_route field is returned null for the Judge rather than answered — and the driver's contemporaneous message to the rider (MSG-05011-003) describes the same PIE accident. On the road, type and window the artifact itself carries, the advisory intersects the recommended route.",
      "evidence_ids": ["EV-ADVIS-05011-01", "EV-TRIP-05011", "EV-CHAT-05011"],
      "clause_ids": ["POL-RD-23"],
      "relies_on": "evidence[EV-ADVIS-05011-01].payload.derived.v7",
      "asserted_weight": 1.0
    },
    {
      "text": "The driver informed the rider of the deviation and the rider agreed to it. MSG-05011-003 reads 'Accident on PIE after Adam Rd, I exit Eng Neo and go Bukit Timah ok?' and MSG-05011-004 answers 'ok can'; POL-RD-21 makes that acknowledgment an agreed deviation. The rider's later claim that 'he did not ask me before turning' is contradicted by his own in-app reply. I disclose that EV-CHAT-05011 is IMPAIRED — weight_multiplier 0.4, issue code CROSS_SOURCE_CONFLICT — and the impairment goes only to which of that entry's two clocks is right, not to the words exchanged, which are identical on both sources.",
      "evidence_ids": ["EV-CHAT-05011"],
      "clause_ids": ["POL-RD-21"],
      "asserted_weight": 0.4
    },
    {
      "text": "The notice came before the point of deviation, as POL-RD-21 requires. The deviation is detected at 08:12:19 and the first Dunearn Road fix is at 08:12:07 (EV-TRIP-05011, EV-GPS-05011), while the driver-device timestamp on MSG-05011-003 is 08:10:49 and that same entry records read_at 08:11:13 — both before the turn. The 08:14:19 delivered_at is the lone outlier on that entry (the pre-pass notes every other entry agrees within 3 s, including this device's own MSG-05011-001 and MSG-05011-002, so a device-wide clock skew is excluded), and on the face of the entry a read receipt cannot post-date delivery by three minutes. The coherent reading of the entry is the device clock: notice before the deviation, with the rider's 'ok can' at 08:14:39 given while the vehicle was still on the diverted road (deviation rejoined 08:22:49). EV-CHAT-05011 is impaired — weight 0.4, CROSS_SOURCE_CONFLICT — and that is the issue I am asking the Judge to resolve, not to ignore.",
      "evidence_ids": ["EV-CHAT-05011", "EV-TRIP-05011", "EV-GPS-05011"],
      "clause_ids": ["POL-RD-21"],
      "relies_on": "evidence[EV-CHAT-05011].payload.messages[MSG-05011-003]",
      "asserted_weight": 0.4
    },
    {
      "text": "The case fits POL-RD-24 row (a) — traffic-justified, rider informed and agreed, deviation over 1 km — so the ruling is NO_ACTION. Under POL-GEN-03 NO_ACTION is party-relative, and on this record it is the driver's outcome: the rider is the filer, the fare breakdown shows payment_status CHARGED and refund_issued_sgd 0.0 (EV-FARE-05011), so leaving the present state standing leaves the metered charge exactly where it is and moves nothing back to the rider.",
      "evidence_ids": ["EV-FARE-05011", "EV-TRIP-05011"],
      "clause_ids": ["POL-RD-24", "POL-GEN-03"],
      "asserted_weight": 1.0
    },
    {
      "text": "However the informing question falls, the matrix caps the money. The excess distance fare under POL-RD-24 is the deviation distance times the per-km rate, without surge: 1.60 km x 0.72 SGD = 1.15 SGD (EV-FARE-05011, derived.money.excess_distance_fare_sgd). That single figure is the whole of what rows (b) and (d) return, and row (a) returns nothing; no row returns the trip fare, and the surge of 7.65 SGD and the time fare of 6.21 SGD are outside the excess-distance formula. The 37.55 SGD the rider claims as the full fare cannot be awarded in whole on any application of the clause.",
      "evidence_ids": ["EV-FARE-05011", "EV-TRIP-05011"],
      "clause_ids": ["POL-RD-24"],
      "relies_on": "fare_breakdown.derived.money.excess_distance_fare_sgd",
      "asserted_weight": 1.0
    },
    {
      "text": "The impairment on the chat log does not cap the whole case at 0.4. The fact that the driver messaged the rider in-trip and the rider answered is also carried by the trip record's own derived.messages_during_trip listing made under POL-RD-21 (MSG-05011-003 from the driver and MSG-05011-004 from the rider), and EV-TRIP-05011 is COMPLETE at weight 1.0. Under POL-GEN-02(2) the weight for a fact two artifacts carry is read at the highest of them; the 0.4 attaches to EV-CHAT-05011 (issue code CROSS_SOURCE_CONFLICT) and to the narrow question of which clock on one entry is right — it does not touch the deviation (EV-TRIP-05011, 1.0), the traffic advisory (EV-ADVIS-05011-01, 1.0) or the fare (EV-FARE-05011, 1.0).",
      "evidence_ids": ["EV-TRIP-05011", "EV-CHAT-05011"],
      "clause_ids": ["POL-GEN-02", "POL-RD-21"],
      "relies_on": "trip_record.derived.v7.messages_during_trip",
      "asserted_weight": 1.0
    },
    {
      "text": "Nothing here removes the case from the AI or raises the confidence bar. The contested amount is 37.55 SGD, inside POL-GEN-22's 10.00 to 50.00 SGD band where an AI ruling stands at 0.80 confidence; neither profile carries a fraud flag; no safety indicator appears in a trip that ran to completion at 08:29:07; and POL-RD-25's 2 km limb is not switched on (route_deviation.thresholds.ai_ruling_max_deviation_applied is false) — and a 1.60 km deviation would sit under 2 km in any event. The artifacts carrying the deviation, the traffic advisory and the fare are all COMPLETE at weight 1.0.",
      "evidence_ids": ["EV-TRIP-05011", "EV-FARE-05011", "EV-ADVIS-05011-01"],
      "clause_ids": ["POL-GEN-22", "POL-RD-25"],
      "relies_on": "authority.required_confidence",
      "asserted_weight": 1.0
    }
  ]
}

